"""
The tire friction law of `Chassis.Wheel.TireFriction` as a signal block: the friction coefficient
`y` against the longitudinal slip ratio `u`, to plot the characteristic or feed a controller model.

Ports: `u` the slip ratio, negative while braking; `y` the friction coefficient for the reference
road, with the sign of the slip.

Assumptions: those of `Chassis.Wheel.TireFriction`, whose parameters and defaults it shares with
the `Slip` tire.
"""
component TireFrictionCurve
  extends BlockComponents.Interfaces.SISO
  extends VehicleComponents.Chassis.Wheel.TireFriction
relations
  s = u
  y = mu_ref
metadata {
  "Dyad": {
    "icons": {"default": "dyad://VehicleComponents/Chassis/Wheel/Helpers/TireFrictionCurve.svg"}
  }
}
end
